 would  say that omix data analysis as you know  uh is something that you can apply to  many many vast areas uh in biology  uh  not just uh cancer not just astrobiology  but actually any possible field that you  can think of  so that is something that i really like  about this particular area that once you  have picked up this particular skill you  can apply it to any research area of  your interest  so yeah thank you so much um  i would  love to take questions if you have any  and you can always contact me on my  email  great thank you very much urja  and subrajeet was very nice to hear your  presentations and we hope that we will  still see you soon again and  hear about the progress  um in conclusion of these great  presentations i want to share a little  bit more information  on how any one of you  can actually join the research  fellowship program  and participate in a research study  using computational tools and one of  these opportunities is a research  fellowship program run by pine biotech  so  the onyx logic research fellowship  is a program designed around  computational biology  for those that are interested not to  just learn and acquire skills but  actually develop a research study  and the research fellowship program is  designed to provide support and guidance  and what i want to do in today's brief  description of this program is explain  how does it actually work and how you  can get started  so as you heard today  many collaborators from today's speakers  were here to offer  their perspective on bioinformatics  different areas of biology and our close  collaboration with these organizations  allows us to apply  kind of a case study design to this  program so i'm really excited about uh  kind of working with a lot of the  experts in the field and being able to  make this an opportunity that anybody  can access so what in in this section  what i want to do is briefly describe  what is the research fellowship program  how to join us this fall uh how to  submit a project on the omixlogic portal  and what makes a project stand out so  first of all where are we in terms of  our program so we are working primarily  in the u.s but we do have a lot of  collaborations outside including india  and africa as you have heard in the  beginning of today's program and overall  we've had a sizable experience working  with over 15 000 participants across 162  countries so we really are agnostic  about where you live and obviously that  is because we are online and so you can  join this program virtually the program  really consists of tools for big data  analysis so we heard today  jio was mentioning how they decided to  work on viruses instead of let's say  human data  that is a typical challenge many studies  after they exceed a few samples and  large genomes you don't have tools you  run out of space you run out of ram and  so we provide that infrastructure to run  your analysis on scale  the second component that we provide is  mentorship it's really more than just  having somebody to ask a question it's  somebody that can understand what you're  trying to do and guide you with not as a  teacher right not as somebody that  actually trains you but as a mentor  somebody that can oversee make  suggestions point you in the right  direction and finally we provide  training because many people see a gap  between where they are  and the skills they need to be able to  meaningfully analyze data we provide  organized schedule training for you to  go through independently asynchronously  on your own time learn about different  types of omics data learn about  different approaches apply different  types of algorithms and therefore kind  of develop your skills and so briefly  let me first talk about some of these  resources that we provide as a part of  this program and as a part of some of  the other programs that we do as well  so one of these resources is the server  t-bioinfo platform  and the comics logic portal so you  probably all have already seen on the  symposium page right on top you have a  menu  on that menu if you click on the logo  you will go to the main omixlogic portal  just by registering there for free you  will have access to a lot of free  resources that you can try out and  explore some of the other materials that  we have after 24 hours of being on that  portal you will also get demo access to  the t by info platform and as you've  seen today there are many exciting new  features that are kind of coming out on  this platform and we also will be  showcasing them once they are ready but  already many areas of our mix data are  available for analysis on that platform  now the portal includes a personal  profile and as somebody who wants to do  research this is the place to start  anybody who is entering this field in  bioinformatics has to build up their  profile and they have to do it by  showcasing what have you achieved so if  you ask any scientist what does that  result in publications poster  presentations etc we've modeled our  profile around the same idea allowing  you to see how much you have learned  what are the courses and the programs  you're involved in and build out your  profile with relevant project  presentations now if you don't know  anything at all about a particular  interest area that you have and would  like to learn we provide  scheduled programs guided by mentors  where you can learn  synchronously by joining live sessions  and also utilize online resources so we  have a lot of asynchronous courses  starting from the very beginning and  ultimately leading you to complete  sessions with practice and so after  completing a number of those you can  interact with the mentors and you can  actually complete those areas of  specialization and earn points and so  that's another metric that we use to  communicate with the students and with  the mentors that we have because  ultimately we have a process in mind we  want everyone who wants to be  mentored who wants to do independent  research to be ready for that right not  to come with nothing to offer but come  with some basic skills that you can  showcase and so you can do that by  building up your profile and showing  what courses you have completed now we  also provide  a number of other opportunities that i  want to talk about after this but before  i do i want to ask all of you that had  the patience to stay up until now  to actually uh join us  and our mentors on our social media  platforms  so we have a group on linkedin where you  will find all of our mentors and all the  different connections that you've seen  today we try to invite all of them to  join there if you want to find their  information how to contact them you will  find them in this group so please join  on linkedin and on facebook we have two  places where we have sizable groups of  relevant contacts if you want to get  involved in these kinds of opportunities  so please join those  so as i mentioned uh you know this is  the place where you can build your  profile on learn and then connect with  mentors and through our program we'll  facilitate introductions and make  meaningful introductions with mentors if  you would like to join  um yes you're welcome to join the groups  the group on linkedin  so  what is the training part of what we do  first of all we have some basic  coursework that you can learn about  bioinformatics and what it includes  genomics transcriptomics metagenomics  epigenomics and data science how to work  with data how to code an r in python how  to run big data analysis pipelines how  to do data wrangling and visualization  right so all of those things are covered  in that portion as well  then we have specialized training  including next generation sequencing  rna-seq analysis or single cell analysis  and a lot of similar courses that you  can either take asynchronously or guided  by a person  finally we provide introductory projects  that you can take to understand a  particular domain like the source code  ii i saw a lot of questions today about  what will be the impact of a mutation or  how will the mutation affect  transmission or things like that so we  cover a lot of those questions using  publicly available data and publications  to try to answer those based on the data  that is available  now as i mentioned a lot of that is not  possible on your own laptop and so  that's why as a part of this program you  and as a part of just registering  actually on the portal you get access to  our big data analysis platform so there  you have access to various processing  tools statistical analysis tools  different types of machine learning  models as well as more advanced kind of  sections for multinomics integration and  biological interpretation  now after this you're ready for the  fellowship after the basic training what  is essentially the fellowship itself  the fellowship is how to go beyond that  and that's where you get an opportunity  to spend three months or six months to  work on an independent project that you  design that you essentially come up with  a topic you then find the data set  perform literature review and work with  the mentor to complete it what does it  mean to complete it  completing it means that you present  that to your peers  and experts for feedback so as you know  we kind of rely on signs published in  peer-reviewed journals well peer review  is an important part that essentially  combines working with others and then  submitting your findings for credit  critique  questions and and feedback and so that's  essentially the outcome of this program  now many people struggle with the first  part of that path and the first part  part is finding a topic for your project  or choosing a topic for a project and so  what we recommend is kind of thinking  about it as the intersection of three  different areas a topic that you know  and care about  something that will be interesting to an  audience and something that has  available data you can actually find  data sets that describe that and provide  you with data  so after you do that you might want to  go through some examples and we provide  a number of different practical examples  that you can go through such as  epigenetics of asthma modeling precision  treatment of breast cancer  deep  sourcing sequencing of poliovirus as we  heard today from raoul  different types of ecological projects  analysis of the changing immune  responses in cancer for immunotherapy  microbiome biomarkers from the american  gut microbiome project whole  transcriptome profiling of cancer tumors  and mouse pdx models deregulation of  subcellular networks in cancer patients  using the cancer genome atlas different  types of biotechnology  agriculture  neuroscience virology and finally your  own project so after surveying some of  the projects and kind of understanding  how they were organized now you are  ready to start working on your own  project  but just choosing a topic like oncology  or virology or even extremophiles is not  enough  as you have seen in today's  presentations what makes a project stand  out  part of it is  what are you focusing on and so an  important part of what you can focus on  it comes from literature comes from the  body body of research work conducted by  others where you can review available  publications and you can understand what  they cover and where are those gaps and  unanswered questions or controversy or  debates where there's disagreement and  gaps in current research and that can  help you make your hypothesis more  specific and essentially define  your unique question  then we have some resources that we can  help you with to try and find data sets  to try and address that gap or  controversy with a data set and so as  you know there's millions of data sets  out there that you can survey and  identify something that might lead you  in the right direction  obviously that's not easy and so that's  why  we have a 