 hear  about some of the other programs that  we've conducted where multiple students  work together on poster presentations  either together with our team or  independently what does that allow you  to do first of all it allows you to  really practice the skills that you have  learned and try to conduct independent  research but also as you will hear from  urja and many others that you will meet  tomorrow you will see how this helps you  stand out and essentially kind of get  your attention in the field that you  want to be in whether it's  bioinformatics or a particular area of  research in a certain community  and so ultimately many of the people  that we have worked with have went on to  present receive prizes get recognition  and including recognition on our own  portal in situations like these where we  bring together others who are interested  in this field experts students and  others to really provide good feedback  and help them kind of understand what  they can do more with the type of  information the type of research that  they have done now this applies to many  different types of students including  high school students undergraduate  students as well as graduate students  and we've worked with many graduate  students phd and post-docs essentially  helping them transition from learning  bioinformatics to them being able to  apply bioinformatics in a meaningful way  to kind of work through their research  ideas and get meaningful insights maybe  before they generate the data or maybe  knowing what to do with the data they  generate  and also we have worked with a number of  students in high schools in the us  in a lot of the programs that you will  hear about tomorrow students have  reached out to us and have utilized the  resources that we compiled to help them  work through a research project  and some of them even completed a full  phd proposal just working on this kind  of a research fellowship  so  as we conclude i just briefly want to  answer a few common questions that  students have when they hear about this  opportunity  so can this program be  used for the requirement of a university  internship the answer is yes  what is the difference between three and  six months programs the difference is  that if you just want to apply  bioinformatics skills to your project  you only need three months if you want  to  learn about bioinformatics and then do  this you might need a longer time  if you want to complete a full research  study you definitely need at least six  months  how many hours commitment does the  research fellowship require so the  answer to that varies and the answer  varies because some people come from  more of a computational background some  come from more of a biology background  after i'm done you will see some of the  posters that people submitted for the  poster competition  many of them came knowing nothing about  bioinformatics but it took them a longer  time to get up to speed  some of them came with advanced  knowledge of bioinformatics but they  learned new methods and applied them to  an interesting data set  what are the mentorship options so we do  provide several types of mentorship  through the program  one option is just meeting in those  regular meetings with a trainer and a  mentor that can provide you with some  general guidelines  another opportunity is to work with a  mentor one-on-one on a project of your  own where a mentor essentially helps you  figure out what to do  and the final option is the other way  around is to join a project that is  organized by somebody else  which means that an expert says i want  to study this question and i would like  you to help so those are the three  options that are available  can you choose any topic for your  analysis the answer is yes  can you participate in group projects  again the answer is yes we have many  examples for those that work together  with their faculty for example or with  the whole class  and then finally pricing payment options  and scholarships so let me just briefly  show you where you can find all of that  information  so if you're already signed up on the  learnomicslogic.com portal  you can quickly go and explore the  courses that i talked about but right  here under programs  you will find some  programs that we offer and if you search  here if you don't find it right here you  can search right here  and you will see research fellowship  and under the research fellowship you  will find all of the information that  you need including our upcoming dates  that we will post by tomorrow for when  this will start because the current  batch is ending on august 30th  so i welcome all of you to explore this  and kind of understand how it works if  you have any questions feel free to  reach out to us at marketing  pine dot bio
 

